{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966784,"nonce":"WfAdw1QoTWcCkBV9r/eEh4DBE2c=","title":"cn::context_menu / cn::dropdown_menu / cn::menubar item click handlers ran `cb()` BEFORE","message":"The cn::context_menu / cn::dropdown_menu / cn::menubar item-click handler structure was:\n\n```rust\n.on_click(move |_| {\n    if !item_disabled \u0026\u0026 !has_submenu {\n        if let Some(ref cb) = item_on_click {\n            cb();                        // user callback\n        }\n        root_handle.close();             // cascade-close THIS menu + everything above it\n    }\n});\n```\n\nThe developer comment in `node_editor_demo.rs` rationalised this ordering as: \"The event-drain runs on the next frame, by which point the menu has finished closing — the dialog then mounts into a clean stack.\" That assumption is **false** — `State::set` (used by `editor.push_event` → `events_rev.set(next)`) is consumed synchronously by Stateful subscribers when they're already in scope. The whole chain `cb() → push_event → drainer's on_state → confirm_delete_nodes → cn::dialog().show() → OverlayStack::push` runs **within `cb()`'s execution**, ALL BEFORE `root_handle.close()` is reached.\n\nTrace from `node_editor_demo` Delete action proving it:\n\n```\npush:      handle=2 kind=Dialog stack_len=1-\u003e2 has_enter_motion=true\nclose_with_reason: handle=1 idx=0 reason=Programmatic entries_above_to_unwind=[2]\n```\n\nThe dialog (handle=2) was pushed first, then the menu's (handle=1) `close_with_reason` saw the dialog in `entries_above_to_unwind` and cascaded `UnwindFromBelow` to kill it. Dialog never appeared.\n\n\nReverse the order at every cn item-click site — `root_handle.close()` BEFORE `cb()`:\n\n```rust\n.on_click(move |_| {\n    if !item_disabled \u0026\u0026 !has_submenu {\n        root_handle.close();\n        if let Some(ref cb) = item_on_click {\n            cb();\n        }\n    }\n});\n```\n\nAt the time `close_with_reason(menu, Programmatic)` runs, `entries_above_to_unwind` is empty (or contains only overlays opened before the click — typically nothing for a fresh menu interaction). Any overlay subsequently pushed by `cb()` lands at the top of the stack and is safe — the cascade computation has already happened.\n\n`close_with_reason` only marks `exiting = true` synchronously; the menu still renders through its exit animation, so users see the close + dialog enter happening simultaneously, which is the desired UX anyway.\n\n\n- [`crates/blinc_cn/src/components/context_menu.rs`](crates/blinc_cn/src/components/context_menu.rs) — primary site\n- [`crates/blinc_cn/src/components/dropdown_menu.rs`](crates/blinc_cn/src/components/dropdown_menu.rs) — same pattern\n- [`crates/blinc_cn/src/components/menubar.rs`](crates/blinc_cn/src/components/menubar.rs) — same pattern\n\nAlso clarified the misleading comment in [`examples/blinc_app_examples/examples/node_editor_demo.rs`](examples/blinc_app_examples/examples/node_editor_demo.rs) at the Delete arm — the event-drain-defer trick was working around this exact bug; with the cn fix, the event indirection is just for symmetry with keyboard / toolbar delete paths, not for ordering correctness.\n\n\nAny menu item that synchronously triggers an overlay mount (dialog, popover, sheet, drawer, hover-card spawned imperatively) will appear to \"do nothing\" — the overlay opens for one frame inside the cascade and is killed before the user perceives it. Affects:\n\n- `confirm_delete_nodes` / `confirm_delete_connection` / `confirm_delete_group` in `node_editor_demo`\n- Any cn-host code that opens a `cn::dialog` / `cn::sheet` / `cn::drawer` directly from a context-menu item callback\n- Any cn-host code that uses an `editor.push_event`-style indirection where the drainer subscriber is a Stateful registered before the menu opened\n\n\nPromoted both `OverlayStack::push` and `OverlayStack::close_with_reason` traces to `info!` temporarily and added per-step traces along the demo's delete chain. The killer signal was `entries_above_to_unwind=[\u003cdialog_handle\u003e]` on the menu's close — proved the close cascade was eating the dialog.\n\nAfter confirming the fix, traces reverted to `trace!` (push) and removed entirely (close + demo). Recipe for future \"overlay opens then immediately closes\" bugs: add `info!` to push + close_with_reason with `entries_above_to_unwind` dump; reproduce; revert.","files":null}]}